Congratulations!  Especially that soon after the last one…

A few minor points I'd like to mention, and maybe general directions
that might make future priest games different from this one:

2014-11-07 09:11 — elina.mustonen@gmail.com:
> I read a lot of spellbooks (and as the result of that had a lot of spells 
> that were useless to me) in order to get the spells I wanted: remove curse, 
> identify, and magic mapping
Here you might want to consider using some of those you already had —
especially on Astral.  I'll point out some possible uses below.

> Your inventory
>   a - a rustproof +6 mace (weapon in hand)
Expert alternatives for the starting mace are the somewhat better
morning star, and of course training with the low-damage war hammer if
you want to sacrifice (neutral) or wish for Mjollnir.  Or consider
getting crowned if you want to unrestrict an additional skill slot…

>   b - a blessed greased fireproof +1 cloak of magic resistance (being worn)
The robe for spellcasting has been mentioned before — if you don't care
about instant spell access or have everything you need at 0% failure,
this is of course of no relevance.

>   m - a ring of free action (on left hand)
>   V - a ring of conflict
>   Y - a ring of levitation (on right hand)
Conflict can be really helpful with the crowds on Astral — but not
everybody likes that strategy.

>   Wands
>   l - a magic lamp (lit) // The only magic lamp I found
The light source can, over the whole game, be even more of a help than
an additional wish, especially after the castle…  And you can't wish for it.

>   y - the Candelabrum of Invocation (7 candles attached)
This gives more light than the lamp — useful for jumping on Astral.

>   X - a can of grease (0:14) // I have no idea why I kept this around
Generally it is not a bad idea to grease your stuff.  It provides 1½
additional barriers to sea monsters / mind flayers / rust.  But past
Water you are certainly right.

> Contents of the bag of holding:
>   an amulet of life saving
Worth a turn keeping at least one or two outside the bag…

>   13 K-rations
These are generally judged sufficient to deal with Famine.  And
preferable to all the other food because they have a good nutrition
value and can still be eaten in a single turn.

>   9 blessed scrolls of remove curse
>   11 diluted potions of full healing
>   12 potions of holy water
Might be a good idea to keep at least one of each outside the bag for
immediate access (weapon/bag cursed by Rodney, unexpected hitpoint loss,
etc).

> Spells known in the end
Now this is where it gets really interesting.  Re-reading some of the
starred spells might provide access to more options, especially on Astral:

>       Name               Level    Category     Fail
>   a - light                  1    divination     0%
>   b - remove curse           3*   clerical       0%
Obvious — it may be a good idea to check its timeout before entering the
Planes.

>   c - identify               3    divination     0%
>   d - magic mapping          5    divination     0%
>   e - extra healing          3*   healing        0%
>   f - restore ability        4*   healing       38%
>   g - slow monster           2*   enchantment    0%
Can make the difference for a successful escape with fast monsters in
mid-game, especially at 0% failure.

>   h - dig                    5*   matter        70%
>   i - force bolt             1*   attack         0%
>   j - detect treasure        4*   divination     0%
Can save your potions for alchemy.  Probably not needed this game, though.

>   k - levitation             4*   escape        47%
An alternative to the ring, but without a ring finger.

>   l - knock                  1*   matter         0%
I like its counterpart, wizard lock, for blocking off corridors with no
doors and for creating locked closets.

>   m - healing                1*   healing        0%
>   n - cure sickness          3*   healing        0%
>   o - cancellation           7*   matter       100%
>   p - drain life             2*   attack         0%
Interesting not only for permanently weakening some powerful enemies in
mid-game, but also for getting a weapon from +6 to +5 for safe
re-enchantment to +7.

>   q - create monster         2*   clerical       0%
More sacrifice fodder…

>   r - teleport away          6*   escape        88%
>   s - jumping                1*   escape         0%
More useful than it may seem, especially together with a wand of
teleport and the lit Candelabrum…

>   t - protection             1*   clerical       0%
>   u - stone to flesh         3*   healing        0%
>   v - turn undead            6*   clerical      59%
>   w - haste self             3*   escape         0%
Can be used together with jumping boots on Astral, when the jumping
spell is not available.

>   x - cause fear             3*   enchantment    0%
>   y - detect unseen          3*   divination     0%
>   z - sleep                  1*   enchantment    0%
Nice to make a barrier against more powerful monsters behind it.

